<title>GREECE: GREEK XIOSBANK KEEPS LENDING RATES UNCHANGED.</title>
<headline>GREEK XIOSBANK KEEPS LENDING RATES UNCHANGED.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Xiosbank, which recently completed a 4.4 billion drachma IPO, will keep its business credit loan rate unchnaged at 17.0 percent from Apr 29 to May 4, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Its XiosAlma deposit account which pays interest monthly will offer an annual yield of 9.92 percent over the same period, it said.</p>
<p>--Angelos Kiosklis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
